{
  "fixture": "vat-return-month",
  "description": "The VAT return can be drawn for a single month, because for most businesses that IS the filing period. The projection took `year` and `quarter`, plus `asOf` for a cut-off date — so a quarterly filer was served and a monthly one was not, and monthly filing is not an edge case: it is mandatory wherever the previous year's tax exceeded a threshold (Germany: 9,000 EUR since 2025, § 18 Abs. 2 UStG), which any mid-sized business passes. The workaround an app would have to invent — two cumulative calls and subtract — is exactly the arithmetic it must not do: under cash-basis taxation and with reversals the difference of two cumulative figures is not the period's figure. `datevExport` already had fromPeriod/throughPeriod, so the shape existed in the house. Asking for a month AND a quarter is refused rather than silently preferring one, and neither given still means the whole year.",
